projects.description:
Quip Network is a base layer protocol that adds post-quantum security to existing blockchains and forms a decentralized infrastructure for quantum computing.

It presents QUIP as secure, composable transaction inputs, similar to enhanced vaults that package classical assets with post-quantum signatures using algorithms like WOTS+ to protect against future quantum attacks.

Users deposit funds into contracts or wallets with QUIP support, creating states for proposals, approvals, claims, and timeouts, enabling atomic cross-chain operations without modifying underlying chains.

Key components include:

Seamless integration with networks like Bitcoin or Ethereum via wallet extensions or smart contracts, supporting compatibility without protocol changes;

The QUIP token for incentivizing validation, staking, nominations, and quantum task execution;

Validators (full nodes) and canary nodes (lightweight attestation);

Quantum clusters performing verifiable quantum tasks (e.g., hash mining, key recovery) using classical or quantum processors.
